From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:30:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] R06 candidate: the scan's key takes each rotation as one
 funnel shift

FrobeniusCanon::canon_in_place found the least rotation of a key's
normal coordinates by n - 1 chained rotate-and-min steps, four vector
instructions each.  On AVX-512 VBMI2 each rotation is now one vpshldq of
the coordinate word written twice, top-aligned, so every rotation comes
from the same two words and costs a shift and a minimum.  The value is
the same for every word (tested against the chained kernel and the
scalar scan for every n from 2 to 63); KIC_CANON_KERNEL=chain keeps the
chained kernel as the same-binary control.

